.TH TLSHELLOTEST 1
.SH NAME
tlshellotest \- probe: real TLS 1.2 ClientHello/ServerHello round trip
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tlshellotest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tlshellotest
is a disposable probe, not a real TLS client. It is staged step 4 of
.IR doc/ssl-modernization-plan.md :
just enough of a TLS 1.2 handshake to confirm a hand-built ClientHello
this tree can produce is accepted by a real server, and that server
answers with the cipher suite and key-exchange curve this tree's plan
already measured. It stops there \(em no key derivation, no
.BR ClientKeyExchange ,
no
.BR Finished ,
no record decryption.
.PP
It hand-rolls the wire encoding directly rather than porting 9front's
.B tlshand.c
.RI ( msgSend / msgRecv
is a generic message-marshalling and record-layer abstraction shared
by every handshake message type and by real record encryption \(em
porting it whole is a much bigger unit of work than this milestone
needs). The extension set, order, and cipher/curve/signature-algorithm
ID values come from two real sources: 9front's own
.B tlsClientExtensions()
/
.B makeciphers()
in
.IR libsec/port/tlshand.c ,
and a live
.B "openssl s_client -tls1_2 -msg -state"
capture against bsky.social saved at
.IR doc/fixtures/bsky-tls12-handshake.txt ,
parsed byte-for-byte before being trusted.
.PP
Two checks, in order:
.IP 1.
.B Offline:
build a ClientHello, then parse the bytes back out with the same
field layout, and confirm every field round-trips \(em version, empty
session id, the exact cipher list, and the exact extension set/order/
content (SNI, supported_groups, ec_point_formats,
signature_algorithms). No network involved.
.IP 2.
.B Live:
dial a real bsky.social IP by literal address
.RI ( dialtest (1)
found
.B /net/cs
doesn't resolve names in this emu instance \(em a separate, tracked
gap; SNI only needs the hostname string, not working DNS), send the
ClientHello, and parse the real
.BR ServerHello ,
.BR Certificate ,
.BR ServerKeyExchange ,
and
.B ServerHelloDone
that come back. Confirms the negotiated cipher suite is one of the
two this tree's plan measured
.RI ( TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
or
.IR TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305 )
and the negotiated curve is X25519.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tlshellotest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR dialtest (1),
.IR x25519test (1)
.SH BUGS
This is scaffolding for one measurement, not the first draft of a
real client: it hardcodes one host, one looked-up-by-hand IP, and a
narrower cipher/extension set than a real browser sends, has no
argument handling, does not verify the server's certificate chain
(reading the chain here is not verifying it \(em see the plan doc's
own gap section), and does not check the ServerKeyExchange signature
at all. It should be deleted or absorbed once the real client (a
proper port of
.BR tlshand.c )
lands and needs its own connection-establishment code.
